    slug: "imeasure",
    name: "iMeasure: Measure & Level",
    tagline: "Ruler, level, compass & more",
    description:
      "iMeasure turns the sensors already in your phone into a pocket toolkit. Eleven tools behind one dark HUD interface, and every one of them works offline.",
    longDescription:
      'iMeasure turns the sensors already in your phone into a pocket toolkit. Eleven tools behind one dark HUD interface, and every one of them works offline.\n\n—— The tools ——\n\nSCREEN RULER\nMeasure small objects directly against your screen, in metric or imperial, horizontally or vertically.\n\nLEVEL\nA bubble level and a bullseye level driven by the accelerometer, for hanging a picture or checking a shelf.\n\nCOMPASS\nA magnetometer heading dial.\n\nPROTRACTOR\nA gyroscope-backed dial for measuring angles, with lock and reset.\n\nBAROMETER\nPressure, derived altitude, a weather read and a trend line. Falls back gracefully on devices with no pressure sensor.\n\nPEDOMETER\nLive step counting for a walking session.\n\nUNIT CONVERTER\nSix categories — length, weight, temperature, area, volume and speed — with accurate factors and proper temperature formulas rather than naive ratios.\n\nNOISE METER\nA sound-level gauge with a reference scale.\n\nAI COACH\nA chat assistant backed by an on-device knowledge base that explains which tool to use and how to get an accurate reading.\n\n—— Built for real use ——\n\n• Dark neon HUD designed to stay readable in a workshop or outdoors\n• Metric and imperial throughout, remembered between sessions\n• Dark and light themes\n• Sign-in is optional — tap "Continue as guest" and every tool is available\n\n—— Honest about accuracy ——\n\nThese readings come from consumer phone sensors. They are good enough for DIY, teaching and quick checks, and they are not calibrated instruments. Do not rely on them where a wrong measurement is expensive or unsafe.',
