    slug: "milemaster",
    name: "iMileMaster",
    tagline: "GPS mileage log for taxes",
    description:
      "MileMaster records the miles you drive and turns them into a mileage log you can file.",
    longDescription:
      "MileMaster records the miles you drive and turns them into a mileage log you can file.\n\nRECORDING A DRIVE\nStart a drive and MileMaster follows your GPS position, adding up the distance between fixes as you go. It throws away readings that are too inaccurate, too small to be real movement, or too fast to be plausible, so the total reflects the road rather than GPS noise. When you stop, you pick what the drive was for and it is saved. Recording runs while the app is open: MileMaster does not track you in the background and does not detect drives by itself.\n\nADDING A TRIP BY HAND\nAny drive can be entered or corrected manually. Type the miles directly, or give a start and end odometer reading and let the app take the difference. Each trip carries a date, a from and to label, a purpose and notes. Trips can be edited or swiped away later.\n\nDEDUCTIONS\nBusiness, medical and charity miles are rated with the IRS figures published for the tax year each trip falls in, and the app names the notice each rate came from. Personal miles are logged but not counted. You can override any year's rates and reset them again. This build ships the published rates for 2023, 2024 and 2025; for a later year it applies the most recent rate it has and tells you on screen that it is doing so. MileMaster is a record-keeping tool and not tax advice.\n\nYOUR LOG\nThe dashboard totals your miles and deduction for the month, the year, or all time. Stats breaks the last week into a bar chart and splits your miles by purpose. Export hands a PDF report and a CSV of the same trips to the share sheet.\n\nPRIVACY\nTrips are stored in a database on this device and are never uploaded. There is no account, no sign-in and no server. The start and end address labels come from the operating system's own geocoder, and where that is unavailable the trip simply keeps its coordinates. There are no ads and nothing to buy.",
