    repo: "MyCard",
    slug: "mycard",
    name: "iMyCard",
    tagline: "Encrypted wallet on your phone",
    description:
      "MyCard is a private wallet. Everything you put in it is encrypted on your device and unlocked with your face, fingerprint, or device passcode.",
    longDescription:
      'MyCard is a private wallet. Everything you put in it is encrypted on your device and unlocked with your face, fingerprint, or device passcode.\n\nWHAT YOU CAN KEEP\n44 card types across seven groups — payment and loyalty cards, ID documents and passports, travel and event passes, business cards, digital keys, notes, tasks and reminders. Add the fields that matter for each one; MyCard knows which are sensitive and masks them until you ask.\n\nHOW IT IS PROTECTED\nThe vault is sealed with AES-256-GCM. GCM authenticates the whole file, so a tampered vault fails to open instead of silently decrypting to garbage. The key lives in the platform secure store, never in the vault file. "Erase all data" deletes every card and destroys the key — there is no copy anywhere else, so that is final.\n\nSTAYS ON YOUR DEVICE\nThere is no account, no cloud sync, and no server. MyCard has no network code at all. Nothing you store can be read by us, because nothing you store ever reaches us.\n\nORGANISE IT\nTag cards, filter by group, archive what you are done with, and search the lot.',
