    repo: "NewsBoard",
    slug: "newsboard",
    name: "iNewsBoard",
    tagline: "Publisher feeds, by topic",
    description:
      "NewsBoard is a reader for news that other people report. It fetches 23 public news feeds from BBC News, BBC Sport, NPR and The Guardian, and shows you what those newsrooms published — their headline, their summary, their byline where they gave one, and the time they published it. NewsBoard writes none of it and changes none of it.",
    longDescription:
      'NewsBoard is a reader for news that other people report. It fetches 23 public news feeds from BBC News, BBC Sport, NPR and The Guardian, and shows you what those newsrooms published — their headline, their summary, their byline where they gave one, and the time they published it. NewsBoard writes none of it and changes none of it.\n\nWHERE EVERY STORY COMES FROM\nEvery article carries the name of the publisher whose feed it arrived in, and opening one gives you a "Read at BBC News" button that takes you to that publisher\'s own page in your browser. Profile lists all four publishers with a link to each of their sites. If a feed does not supply something — a picture, a byline, a summary — that space is left empty rather than filled in.\n\nBY TOPIC\nTechnology, business, science, health, politics, sport, entertainment, environment and world, plus a For You view of everything and a Trending view. Trending here means one thing only: the same story is being carried by more than one of the publishers. There is no popularity score, no view count and no ranking, because nothing in the app measures any of those.\n\nREAD LATER, FOLLOW, SEARCH\nSave any article to read later; saved articles stay on your device. Follow a topic or a hashtag and the Following tab collects matching stories. Search runs across the headlines, summaries, publishers and tags of everything that has loaded.\n\nOFFLINE, HONESTLY\nThe last set of stories NewsBoard successfully downloaded is kept on the device. With no connection it shows that set and says "Offline · showing stories saved 2h ago" above it, so you always know how old what you are reading is. With nothing downloaded yet it tells you the fetch failed and offers a retry, instead of showing you an empty page that looks like a quiet news day.\n\nWHAT IT DOES NOT DO\nNo account, no sign-in. No advertising. No subscription and no in-app purchase — there is no paid tier and nothing is held back. Nothing in NewsBoard is generated: no AI summaries, no rewritten headlines. There is no push notification. Market quotes are not available: opening a stock symbol says so rather than showing a made-up price.',
